Relay sends an HTTP POST to your endpoint for every event you subscribe to.
Payloads are JSON and never larger than 256 KB.

## Signing

Each request carries a `Relay-Signature` header. Compute an HMAC-SHA256
of the raw body with your signing secret and compare it in constant time.
Reject requests whose timestamp is more than five minutes old.

## Timeouts

Your endpoint has 10 s to respond with a 2xx status. Anything else counts
as a failed attempt.

## Retries

Failed deliveries are retried up to 5 times. The delay doubles after
each attempt, starting at 0.5 s and capped at 60 s.

We retry on any 5xx response and on 429 Too Many Requests.

## Ordering

Deliveries for the same subscription are not guaranteed to arrive in order.
