Relay sends an HTTP POST to your endpoint for every event you subscribe to.
Payloads are JSON and never larger than 256 KB.

## Signing

Each request carries a `Relay-Signature` header. Compute an HMAC-SHA256
of the raw body with your signing secret and compare it in constant time.
Reject requests whose timestamp is more than five minutes old.

## Timeouts

Your endpoint has 10 s to respond with a 2xx status. Anything else counts
as a failed attempt.

## Retries

Failed deliveries are retried up to 8 times. Each delay is drawn at
random between zero and a cap that doubles after every attempt, starting
at 0.5 s and never exceeding 60 s. Spreading retries out keeps a
recovering endpoint from being hit by every queued delivery at once.

We retry on any 5xx response, on 408 Request Timeout and on 429 Too Many
Requests. If your endpoint sends a `Retry-After` header we wait exactly
that long instead, up to the same 60 s limit.

## Ordering

Deliveries for the same subscription are not guaranteed to arrive in order.
